   ***Circle Demonstrations***

   - Create `circle` with radius 5.3, color "Blue", and filled `true`.
     - Call `print()`, display color, fill status, radius, area, diameter.
     - Use overloaded `<<` to print circle.

   - Create `circle2` with radius 15.3 using an alternate constructor.
     - Call `print()`, display default color and fill.
     - Change color to "Green" and display again.
     - Show radius, area, diameter.
     - Use `<<` to print `circle2`.

   - Create default `circle3`.
     - Call `print()`, show properties.
     - Set new radius `26.7`, color "Yellow".
     - Use `<<` to print updated `circle3`.

   ***Rectangle Demonstrations***

   - Create `rect1` with width 27.9, height 15.6, color "Red", filled `false`.
     - Call `print()`, display color, fill, width, height, area, perimeter.
     - Use `<<` to print `rect1`.

   - Create `rect2` with width 13.2, height 15.6.
     - Call `print()`, show default color and fill.
     - Change color to "Cyan".
     - Show updated width, height, area, perimeter.
     - Use `<<` to print `rect2`.

   - Create default `rect3`.
     - Call `print()`, show properties.
     - Set height to `26.7`, width to `14.98`, color to "Indigo".
     - Show updated width, height, area, perimeter.
